Registers grove-g1's SIMULATION-ONLY conveyor drag in the vendored unitree_mujoco.

Generated against unitree_mujoco ae6a8403e272733e9996ef59990880330496177f, on top of
001-006 (whose main.cc / CMakeLists.txt context this diff includes), applied in filename
order after 003's RH56E2 hands.

The conveyor manager's own source (conveyor_handler.h/.cc) is COPYed in by the build
scripts and is NOT part of this patch, so this stays a registration hook: an include, a
start, two stops, and one source file added to the target. simulate/src/unitree_sdk2_bridge.h
is untouched.

Started from main() right after grasp_weld, for the same reason grasp_weld is started
there rather than from the bridge thread: this needs sim->mtx and opens no DDS channels.

Stopped at both model-replacement paths (the viewer's Reload button and drag-and-drop)
with a blocking join, before mj_deleteModel, because it caches body and dof ids resolved
against the old model. It is not restarted afterwards, so a reload ends with nothing held.

What it exists for: MuJoCo has no native infinite moving surface, so a scene that wants a
conveyor belt needs something to drag free bodies resting on it. This treats any geom
named `conveyor_belt` (or `conveyor_belt_*`) as a zone and applies a velocity-tracking
force, along that geom's own local +x, to any free-jointed body whose origin falls inside
it. On hardware this file never runs -- a real belt's own motor and friction do this job,
and speed/gain here are properties of the simulated zone, not of any real conveyor.

